(a) the details of approvals granted under the Khelo India Scheme for the development and construction of sports infrastructure in Chhattisgarh;
(b) whether Central Government is planning to establish a State Training Centre, a Sports University in Raipur and a Sports Science Centre in Bilaspur and whether Government is making any efforts to set up a Centre of Excellence for sports in the State; and
(c) the details of budget released by the Central Government to the State for the promotion and development of sports?

(a) the details of financial assistance provided to laboratories in  Chhattisgarh by the Department of Science and Technology (DST) and the Chhattisgarh Council of Science and Technology (CCOST);
(b) the progress made in scientific research relating to agriculture, healthcare (as sickle cell anaemia) and utilisation of local resources in rural areas and tribal districts;
(c) the details of outcomes achieved in this regard; and
(d) the details of digital and technological expansion in the remote areas of the State, including internet connectivity, modernization of science centres such as the Regional Science Centre, Raipur and promotion of technical education?

(a) whether the Ministry has unveiled 'PRAHAAR' as India's first comprehensive 'National Counter-Terrorism Policy and Strategy,' and if so, the date of unveiling and the key pillars thereof;
(b) the specific objectives of 'PRAHAAR' that could not be effectively addressed under the existing counter-terrorism and internal security framework;
(c) the institutional and coordination mechanisms proposed between Central and State agencies for the implementation of this policy; and
(d) the timeline for the operationalization of this strategy and the manner in which the outcomes thereof would be reviewed?

(a) the objectives of the Post-Matric Scholarship (PMS) scheme;
(b) the details of the annual target fixed for providing scholarships under the Post-Matric Scholarship (PMS) scheme to Scheduled Caste (SC) students across the country, State-wise;
(c) the income eligibility criteria for the grant of scholarships; and
(d) the details of the Central assistance released to Chhattisgarh during the last five years and the number of beneficiaries thereof?

(a) the steps taken to strengthen collaboration with industry and technology companies to provide industry-relevant skill training;
(b) whether Government has undertaken measures to promote apprenticeship training under the National Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme (NAPS), if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) support is being provided to apprentices under NAPS-2, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the special initiatives taken to improve participation of women in apprenticeship training and expand apprenticeship opportunities across service sectors, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total quantum of Rural Local Body (RLB) Grants recommended by the Sixteenth Finance Commission for Panchayati Raj Institutions during the award period 2026-31, including Chhattisgarh;
(b) the operational guidelines issued for utilisation of these grants and the priority sectors identified for their deployment;
(c) the strategies being adopted to enhance Panchayats' Own Source Revenue (OSR) mobilisation as discussed at the National Workshop held on 3rd July, 2026; and
(d) the mechanism put in place to monitor effective and timely utilisation of Finance Commission grants by States and Panchayati Raj Institutions in Chhattisgarh?

(a) the major work undertaken under the Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) in the State of Chhattisgarh for the financial, social and economic security of fishermen in the fisheries sector;
(b) the extent to which the incomes of fishermen and fish farmers have increased under the scheme and whether modern technologies and infrastructure, such as cold storage, ice plants and fish transportation are being adopted and the efforts being made to make India a global leader in fish production; and
(c) the major and broad objectives of the scheme and the future phase-wise plans for achieving the same?

(a) whether Government has achieved landmark success in the certification of Government hospitals across the country under the National Quality Assurance Standards (NQAS) and National Accreditation Board for Hospitals & Healthcare Providers (NABH);
(b) the total number of district and State hospitals that have been successfully certified so far across the country;
(c) whether district hospitals and health centres in the State of Chhattisgarh have also performed well in obtaining such quality certification; and
(d) the number of certified facilities in the State at present and the qualitative improvements brought about in public healthcare as a result thereof?

(a) the salient features of the amendments made to Schedule VII to the Companies Act, 2013 to facilitate Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) through zero coupon zero principal instruments;
(b) the framework prescribed for the implementation of CSR through zero coupon zero principal instruments;
(c) the details of the amendments made to the Companies CSR Rules, 2014 for the implementation of CSR through zero coupon zero principal instruments; and
(d) the details of limits prescribed on the expenditure incurred by companies on CSR through zero coupon zero principal instruments?

(a) the State-wise details of the requirement and availability of major fertilizers during the last three Kharif and Rabi seasons;
(b) the details of the system adopted by Government to monitor the movement and distribution of fertilizers down to the district level;
(c) the details of the measures taken to address the shortage of fertilizers and to ensure its timely availability during the Kharif and Rabi seasons; and
(d) the details of the long-term arrangements made to ensure the supply of phosphatic fertilizers and their raw materials?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any measures to operationalize the proposed 'SME Growth Fund' and strengthen equity support for MSMEs;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) progress made under the 'Aatmanirbhar Bharat/Self Reliant India (SRI) Fund' in facilitating equity investment for MSMEs;
(d) whether any mechanism has been developed to improve access to equity financing for MSMEs in aspirational districts and non-metropolitan regions;
(e) if so, the details thereof; and
(f) the manner in which these initiatives are expected to strengthen the growth and competitiveness of MSMEs?

(a) the major policy reforms undertaken during the last one year to strengthen the coal sector including in Chhattisgarh coal regions and support India’s growing energy requirements;
(b) the measures taken to improve coal allocation, logistics, evacuation infrastructure and coordination with the power sector for ensuring uninterrupted fuel supply;
(c) the initiatives undertaken to promote technological innovation, sustainable mining and diversification of coal utilisation through value-added products; and
(d) the roadmap for strengthening the coal sector in alignment with the objectives of Atmanirbhar Bharat and Viksit Bharat@ 2047?

(a) whether Government plans to launch a 'National Digital Skill Mission' for the youth of tribal and rural areas such as Bastar, Sarguja, Kanker and Jashpur in Chhattisgarh;
(b) whether Government is formulating any roadmap to provide free training in subjects like drone operation, data analytics and cybersecurity in these areas;
(c) whether Government will collaborate with the Chhattisgarh Government to train 1 lakh youth annually through initiatives like 'AI Gurukul Program'; and
(d) the efforts being made by Government to develop AI-based solutions for marketing local handicrafts and forest products in rural areas?

(a) whether Government is implementing the National Beekeeping and Honey Mission (NBHM);  
(b) if so, the  details and objectives thereof; and   
(c) the details of the steps taken/proposed to be taken by Government to increase honey production, scientific beekeeping and related advantages for agricultural productivity?

(a) whether complaints submitted by citizens to various central institutions and statutory bodies are not being resolved within the prescribed timeline, resulting in citizens facing unnecessary financial, social, and mental hardships;  
(b) if so, the details of complaints pending beyond the prescribed timeline during the last five years, Ministry-wise and the number of officials against whom the departmental disciplinary action has been taken; and 
(c) whether Government is considering to implement any central legislation or national framework, with a view to provide citizens a statutory right for timely grievance redressal?

(a) the number of nuclear reactors in the country, the current power generation capacity thereof and the measures being taken to augment the same;
(b) the plan to set up a nuclear power project in Chhattisgarh to meet the future energy requirements of the State; and
(c) by when action is proposed to be taken for the mining of uranium deposits in view of the indications thereof in Rajnandgaon and Raigarh districts of the State?

(a) the number of 'black spots' (accident-prone areas) identified on the highways of Chhattisgarh and the steps taken to rectify them;
(b) the status of the availability of trauma centres and ambulance facilities on the National Highways of Chhattisgarh; and
(c) the measures being taken to discourage overloading, identify overloaded vehicles and impose heavy fines on them on the National Highways of Chhattisgarh?

(a) whether Government is aware of the fact that for admission to NRI seats under the Chhattisgarh State quota and the All India quota, an NRI certificate is mandatory and agents misuse the non availability of certificates under the NRI quota;  
(b) whether Government is amending the rules for NRI seats to create a strict online document verification portal to ensure joint online document verification in collaboration with the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare and the Ministry of External Affairs; and 
(c) whether any concrete plan is being prepared for legal action against contractors/intermediaries/private colleges facilitating fake admissions?

(a) whether the 'Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission' (ABDM) successfully established a robust digital ecosystem for paperless and accessible health services in Chhattisgarh; 
(b) the total number of 'ABHA' (Ayushman Bharat Health Account) health ID cards created in the State so far; 
(c) whether digitally linking patients' health records ensured rapid and transparent treatment in hospitals; and 
(d) the progress of the State's hospitals and healthcare professionals in adopting this digital initiative?

(a) whether the Agriculture Infrastructure Fund (AIF) has successfully modernized the post-harvest facilities across Chhattisgarh, including in major agricultural hubs like Baloda Bazar;
(b) the details of new warehouses and cold storage facilities funded in the State;
(c) Government's action plan for increasing the use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) technology in agriculture and promoting drone technology; and
(d) the extent of increase in the income of farmers in Chhattisgarh due the use of these technologies?

(a) whether the Mission envisages use of Artificial Intelligence (AI)-based monitoring systems and digital health tracking;
(b) action plan under this Mission to implement 'Digital Health Records' for Anganwadi Centres and school children, and 'Mother and Child Protection Cards' for pregnant women and children; 
(c) whether Government proposes to prescribe time-bound targets for reducing malnutrition by 70 percent and anaemia by 60 percent by 2035, particularly by prioritizing tribal/aspirational districts and remote areas; and
(d) steps being taken to ensure inter-departmental coordination among concerned Ministries for the effective implementation of the Mission?

(a) whether the 'Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan' has successfully strengthened the administrative capacity of Panchayati Raj Institutions in Chhattisgarh;
(b) the details of the digital infrastructure and training provided to Gram Panchayats;
(c) whether the active promotion of the 'Localization of Sustainable Development Goals' (LSDGs) led to improvements in rural sanitation, health and gender equality; and
(d) the notable development achievements recorded under this framework in the State of Chhattisgarh?

(a) the current status of Kharsia-Parmalkasa Rail Project and the timeline set for its completion;
(b) whether Government has assessed the potential economic and industrial benefits of connecting a key industrial hub such as Baloda Bazar district via this rail route, particularly in the context of cement and mineral transportation; and
(c) whether it is a fact that the construction of this rail route would reduce traffic congestion on the Bilaspur-Raipur main line and lead to estimated annual savings of approximately ?2,520 crore in logistics costs, if so, the steps to be taken by Government to expedite the implementation of the said project?

(a) whether Government is formulating any specific scheme at the national level to develop modern warehouses, processing units and price stabilization mechanisms for farmers of major paddy-producing States such as Chhattisgarh;
(b) whether Government will launch a 'National Crop Price Protection Programme' to provide price deficiency support to farmers in the event of a decline in market prices;
(c) whether there is any plan to utilize satellite monitoring and AI-based analytical systems for forecasting agricultural risks in order to control crop losses in time; and
(d) whether Government will implement it as a pilot project in agriculture-dominated States such as Chhattisgarh?
